    "summary": "Restored intel-core-fixes-2-001's snapshot (a18265e) without features/; the diff check printed nothing and every restored path is owned. step.ts now builds leads in three phases: gatherLeads (a set keyed by (player,type) holding the earliest free trigger, fresh before replacement, and sorted request ids); decide/decideLeads (per player by id: the start rumor first, then entries in type order; one sighting message per player listing its types in type order; every draw keyed by fnv1a64(seed, tick or snapshot tick, player, type) over sorted candidates); and answerRequests (per (player,type) by requestId: covered when a free trigger or the start gave that type; otherwise rumor or sighting for the first request and covered for the rest; the same capped or none for all when nothing is delivered). Added the TargetedRumorResult 'covered'. Narrowed the sighting reason to CarrierSightingReason (fresh|targeted|replacement). A new id listed twice in one batch is taken for its lowest (player,type). validateIntelRules now refuses a carrierRevealTicks that isn't a multiple of carrierIntervalTicks, with a content test. Tests added: phase-2 and phase-3 helpers over every order of three triggers across three types with two carriers per type in contested sectors, plus cover, capped and free-rumor groups, and two players buying one type (both delivered); a ts-expect-error type test for the reason; a scripted step with out-of-type-order requests and contested sectors compared against the fully reversed step; and a black-box property check on the six compressed scenarios that adds purchases, shuffles each step's requests, players and rubbings, and compares messages, outcomes sorted by requestId and hashState. The Checker now also rejects non-sighting reasons and wrong charges. docs/intel.md is updated. Ran from this worktree after npm ci: npm run typecheck (pass), npm run test:unit (595 passed), npm run test:integration (36 passed), npm run build (pass, smoke passed). Expectation changes: 'lift the sighting cap' now expects [covered, sighting] for two same-type requests (it was [sighting, sighting]). The property scenario seed 15 became seed 27, because the keyed draws changed the random paths and seed 27 reaches a several-type message. outcome:covered was added to EXERCISED.",
